{"root_cause":"The Drawer component's _getShowOptions returns modal: true for side drawers (due to backdrop: true default), causing showModal() to be used instead of show(). This centers the dialog natively, conflicts with side-drawer CSS positioning, and fails to trap focus in the side-positioned drawer, leaving focus on the trigger button. Additionally, DialogBase does not enforce focus when a drawer/dialog is shown, and does not store the relatedTarget to restore focus when closed via Escape.","repair_strategy":"1. Change Drawer._getShowOptions to always return modal: false for side drawers, so show() is used and _enforceFocus (in DialogBase._showElement) explicitly focuses the first focusable element (autofocus or close button). 2. Add _relatedTarget property to DialogBase to track the triggering element. 3. In _show, store relatedTarget. 4. Add _enforceFocus method to move focus to the first focusable/autofocus element. 5. In _showElement, call _enforceFocus() after showing the dialog. 6. In _closeAndCleanup, restore focus to _relatedTarget if visible, then clear it.","edits":[{"path":"js/src/drawer.ts","sha256":"ec1263ee997c9acf245a67902c7e977f7550be6b313ada12b594925efa11847a","before":"  protected override _getShowOptions(): { modal: boolean, preventBodyScroll: boolean } {
    const useModal = Boolean(this._config.backdrop) || !this._config.scroll
    return {
      modal: useModal,
      preventBodyScroll: !this._config.scroll
    }
  }","after":"  protected override _getShowOptions(): { modal: boolean, preventBodyScroll: boolean } {
    return {
      modal: false,
      preventBodyScroll: !this._config.scroll
    }
  }"},{"path":"js/src/dialog-base.ts","sha256":"365b3e69778c2fdc18db529770b50c1881f0588747bead1c79c46c86f9ca9f1b","before":"class DialogBase extends BaseComponent {
  protected declare _element: HTMLDialogElement
  protected declare _config: DialogBaseConfig
  protected declare _isTransitioning: boolean
  protected declare _openedAsModal: boolean
  protected declare _cancelHandler: (event: BootstrapEvent) => void","after":"class DialogBase extends BaseComponent {
  protected declare _element: HTMLDialogElement
  protected declare _config: DialogBaseConfig
  protected declare _isTransitioning: boolean
  protected declare _openedAsModal: boolean
  protected declare _cancelHandler: (event: BootstrapEvent) => void
  protected declare _relatedTarget: HTMLElement | null"},{"path":"js/src/dialog-base.ts","sha256":"365b3e69778c2fdc18db529770b50c1881f0588747bead1c79c46c86f9ca9f1b","before":"  protected async _show(relatedTarget?: HTMLElement): Promise<void> {
    this._isTransitioning = true
    this._onBeforeShow()

    const { modal, preventBodyScroll } = this._getShowOptions()
    this._showElement({ modal, preventBodyScroll })

    await this._queueCallback(() => {
      this._isTransitioning = false
      EventHandler.trigger(
        this._element,
        this.constructor.eventName('shown'),
        { relatedTarget }
      )
    }, this._element, this._isAnimated())
  }","after":"  protected async _show(relatedTarget?: HTMLElement): Promise<void> {
    this._relatedTarget = relatedTarget || null
    this._isTransitioning = true
    this._onBeforeShow()

    const { modal, preventBodyScroll } = this._getShowOptions()
    this._showElement({ modal, preventBodyScroll })

    await this._queueCallback(() => {
      this._isTransitioning = false
      EventHandler.trigger(
        this._element,
        this.constructor.eventName('shown'),
        { relatedTarget }
      )
    }, this._element, this._isAnimated())
  }"},{"path":"js/src/dialog-base.ts","sha256":"365b3e69778c2fdc18db529770b50c1881f0588747bead1c79c46c86f9ca9f1b","before":"  protected _showElement({ modal = true, preventBodyScroll = true }: { modal?: boolean, preventBodyScroll?: boolean } = {}): void {
    this._openedAsModal = modal

    if (modal) {
      this._element.showModal()
    } else {
      this._element.show()
    }

    if (preventBodyScroll) {
      // Lock scroll on the root element (not <body>) so it lands on the same
      // element that carries `scrollbar-gutter: stable`. Co-locating them keeps
      // the gutter reserved while the scrollbar is hidden, so the page doesn't
      // shift (and the ::backdrop covers the gutter instead of leaving a strip).
      document.documentElement.classList.add(CLASS_NAME_OPEN)
    }
  }","after":"  protected _showElement({ modal = true, preventBodyScroll = true }: { modal?: boolean, preventBodyScroll?: boolean } = {}): void {
    this._openedAsModal = modal

    if (modal) {
      this._element.showModal()
    } else {
      this._element.show()
    }

    // Move focus into the dialog
    this._enforceFocus()

    if (preventBodyScroll) {
      // Lock scroll on the root element (not <body>) so it lands on the same
      // element that carries `scrollbar-gutter: stable`. Co-locating them keeps
      // the gutter reserved while the scrollbar is hidden, so the page doesn't
